ation**\\n    89→    - Problem: \\\"De Lacey\\\" (9 mentions), \\\"De\\\" (6 mentions), and \\\"old man\\\" (2 mentions) potentially separate\\n    90→    - Evidence: \\\"De Lacey\\\" is the blind father in the cottage. \\\"De\\\" is likely an incomplete extraction. \\\"old man\\\" may refer to De Lacey.\\n    91→    - Location: Name extraction creating incomplete \\\"De\\\" + descriptor resolution for \\\"old man\\\"\\n    92→    - Fix: Improve compound name handling for \\\"De Lacey\\\", \\\"Van Helsing\\\" style names. Merge descriptive references.\\n    93→    - Impact: -0.1 points\\n    94→\\n    95→11. **Inconsistent canonical names using relational descriptors**\\n    96→    - Problem: \\\"my father\\\" and \\\"my mother\\\" used as canonical names instead of \\\"Alphonse Frankenstein\\\" and \\\"Caroline Frankenstein\\\"\\n    97→    - Evidence: Character profiles show \\\"my father\\\" (53 mentions) and \\\"my mother\\\" (10 mentions) as main headings rather than proper names\\n    98→    - Location: Canonical name selection in consensus.py\\n    99→    - Fix: Prefer proper names over relational descriptors when selecting canonical name. The proper name should be canonical, with relational terms as aliases.\\n   100→    - Impact: Usability issue (scoring included in Critical #1 and High #7)\\n   101→\\n   102→### LOW\\n   103→None at this time.\\n   104→\\n   105→## Fix History\\n   106→### Attempt 1: Fixed CLI output path handling\\n   107→**Issue:** CLI ignored explicit `--html` and `--output` flags, creating timestamped directory instead\\n   108→\\n   109→**Fix Applied:**\\n   110→- Modified `src/cli.py` lines 367-368: Added `output_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)` for JSON output\\n   111→- Modified `src/cli.py` lines 397-398: Added `html_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)` for HTML output\\n   112→\\n   113→**Testing:** All 444 tests pass.\\n   114→\\n   115→**Result:** PASSED - CLI now respects explicit output paths\\n   11